{"id":"u-268f97d9-e91b-4c2d-9c07-151f30ae6131","src":"community","title":"Broken in Half","author":"Adam Breton","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/1FHLak-broken-in-half","desc":"Ten weeks. Four days. Two upper, two lower, every muscle hit twice a week. The whole thing is built to put size back on after time off, and it does it by pushing progressive overload instead of chasing heavy singles.\n\nNo low-bar squats. No conventional deadlifts. Hack squats and RDLs do the leg and posterior-chain work with a fraction of the back and joint fatigue. If heavy barbell squatting or pulling has ever lit up your back, hips, or hamstrings, this is built for you. Machines and dumbbells carry most of the load, with bench, hack squat, and RDL as the free-weight anchors.\n\nRunning it is simple. First two weeks, leave 2-3 reps in the tank and work around 60-65%. This matters most if you're coming back from a layoff. Your strength will want to jump ahead of your joints, so let it wait. From week 3, hit the top of every rep range and add weight: 5 lb up top, 10 lb below. \n\nSwap what you need to. Seated or lying leg curl, cable or dumbbell laterals, whatever your gym has and your body likes. Run movements you can load week after week and actually feel where they're supposed to hit. The structure is the point","level":["Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-07-15T13:10:21.121Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper A","Lower A","Upper B","Lower B"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":4}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo